{"name":"Tin Man","hex":"#a4a298","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Tin Man","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["The Tin Woodman, a metallic character in the fictional Land of Oz who travels with Dorothy, the Scarecrow, and the Cowardly Lion to the Emerald City in search of a heart."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Tin_Man"}],"entries":[{"title":"Tin Woodman","blocks":[{"text":"Nick Chopper, the Tin Woodman or the Tin Man, is a character in the fictional Land of Oz created by American author L. Frank Baum. He first appeared in his 1900 book The Wonderful Wizard of Oz and reappeared in many other subsequent Oz books in the series. In late 19th-century America, men made out of various tin pieces were used in advertising and political cartoons. Baum, who was editing a magazine on decorating shop windows when he wrote The Wonderful Wizard of Oz, was inspired to create the Tin Woodman by a figure he had built out of metal parts for a shop display."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f9/Tin_Woodman.png/330px-Tin_Woodman.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tin_Woodman"},{"title":"Tin Man (miniseries)","blocks":[{"text":"Tin Man is a 2007 American television miniseries co-produced by RHI Entertainment and the Sci Fi Channel that was broadcast first in the United States on the Sci Fi Channel in three parts. Starring Zooey Deschanel, Neal McDonough, Alan Cumming, Raoul Trujillo, Kathleen Robertson, and Richard Dreyfuss, the miniseries is a reimagining of the classic 1900 novel The Wonderful Wizard of Oz by L. Frank Baum, with science fiction and additional fantasy elements added. It focuses on the adventures of a small-town waitress named DG who is pulled into a magical realm called the O.Z., ruled by the tyrannical sorceress Azkadellia. Together with her companions Glitch, Raw, and Cain, DG journeys to uncover her memories, find lost connections, and foil Azkadellia's plot to trap the O.Z. in eternal darkness."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/4/45/Tin_Man_poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tin_Man_(miniseries)"},{"title":"Tin","blocks":[{"text":"Tin is a chemical element; it has the symbol Sn and atomic number 50. A metallic-gray metal, tin is soft enough to be cut with little force, and a bar of tin can be bent by hand with little effort. When bent, a bar of tin makes a sound, the so-called \"tin cry\", as a result of twinning in tin crystals."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2b/Sn-Alpha-Beta.jpg/330px-Sn-Alpha-Beta.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tin"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f9/Tin_Woodman.png/500px-Tin_Woodman.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f9/Tin_Woodman.png/1280px-Tin_Woodman.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f9/Tin_Woodman.png/500px-Tin_Woodman.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATin_Woodman.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1d/Tin-Man-poster-Hamlin.jpeg/500px-Tin-Man-poster-Hamlin.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1d/Tin-Man-poster-Hamlin.jpeg/1280px-Tin-Man-poster-Hamlin.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1d/Tin-Man-poster-Hamlin.jpeg/500px-Tin-Man-poster-Hamlin.jpeg?ut